 ## Background
-The concept of combining multiple loss terms for training differentiable rendering models has evolved alongside the development of Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF) and 3D Gaussian Splatting. Early NeRF methods primarily used photometric loss [S1]. As the field advanced, additional constraints such as depth, pose, and semantic information were incorporated to improve robustness and generalization [S2, S5, S6]. The specific formulations of the overall training loss vary significantly depending on the representation (Gaussian, Voxel, Implicit) and the specific task (deblurring, sparse-view reconstruction, open-vocabulary understanding) [S1, S2, S3, S4, S5, S6][S8, S9, unofficial].
